  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#ConnectionTimeLag">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Enumeration of time lag values. Applicable in the context of a connection between two factors. Refers to the time lapse between the incidence of the source factor and the subsequent factor, especially in relation to the interactions from hazard to hazard, hazard to impact, and impact to impact. Example for Increased in extreme heat -&gt; Increased in heat stress: Although the response to heat is immediate, prolonged exposure time is required to generate heat stress, and this duration can vary from hours to days, depending on the element exposed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">connection time lag</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
